{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From the chamber comes the storm</b> — It is possible that it is like 'the chambers of the south' (Job 9:9), the southern direction, as I explained." "<b>And from the scatterings</b> — Some say: it is the northern direction. And some say: constellations. And some say: it is from 'scattered [מזורה] the net' (Ezekiel 12:13), in the sense of far off. And the correct one in my eyes: they are stars, like 'Can you bring forth the scatterings [מזרות] in their season?' (Job 38:32)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:53.219449428Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}